## THE FOUR STALLS

One stall per quadrant. Each party member claims one.

| Quadrant | Position | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Northeast** | Slight elevation, central visibility | Prime foot traffic. First to be seen from the main road. |
| **Northwest** | Near the supply lane entrance | Close to incoming deliveries. First pick on arriving goods. |
| **Southeast** | Adjacent to the craftsmen's quarter | Specialty buyers pass through frequently. |
| **Southwest** | Corner position, widest space | Largest physical footprint. Best for bulk displays and expansion. |

**DM Note:** Party members are free to divide labor however they like day to day — there is no fixed role assignment. If party members cooperate, they are pooling customers. If they compete, each independently tracks earnings. The floor rewards individual totals — the party member with the highest sales wins the ranking, not the group as a whole. Cooperation on procurement and crafting is not only possible, it's the intended path. Credit on the ledger is individual regardless of who gathered or crafted what.

