## STRUCTURE OF A DAY

Each of the five days runs on the same clock. Every round is 5 minutes.

| Time | Block |
|---|---|
| 8:00–9:00 | Free hour — prep, Soren, errands, robbery, alt actions |
| 9:00–12:00 | **Gathering Window A** — Hunt / Forage (Forest Edge) |
| 10:00–1:00 | **Gathering Window B** — Mine / Fish (Underground / Docks) |
| 1:00–4:00 | **Gathering Window C** — Fish / Forage (Docks / Forest Edge) |
| 2:00–5:00 | **Gathering Window D** — Mine / Hunt (Underground / Forest Edge) |
| 5:00–6:00 | Free hour — prep stall, last advertising, Soren |
| 6:00–10:00 | **Market Time** — the Selling Phase |

8:00–6:00 (the **Production Day**) is where Gathering, Robbery, Trading, Crafting, advertising, investigation, and scouting happen. Market Time (6:00–10:00) is the Selling Phase — not round-counted, it runs until that day's customers are processed (see Selling Phase, below, for how many that typically is).

### Round Action Points (RAP)

Every player has **4 RAP per round**, representing minor decisions, conversations, and quick actions within a five-minute window.

**Major Actions** interrupt RAP completely. When a player commits to a Major Action, they announce which round they start and how many rounds it takes. They have no RAP during those rounds. At the end of the final waived round, one die roll determines the outcome.

**Natural 1 on any Major Action check:** Action takes 50% longer (round up). **Natural 20:** Takes 50% less time (round down, minimum 1 round).

**On Failure by 5 or more:** Player still spends the rounds but gains nothing — plus a complication at DM discretion (lost in the forest, attracted unwanted attention, ruined the materials).

