## CORE RULE: WHERE PRODUCTS COME FROM

**Products (Hunt/Fish/Forage/Mine Product) only ever enter play through the Craft Major Action** — performed either by a player or commissioned through an NPC crafter (Commission Craftsperson). No Gathering roll, robbery, trade, scavenging, favor, or daily event ever hands a player a finished Product directly. Crafting takes real time off the clock — that's the cost. In exchange, a Product is worth meaningfully more than the sum of the raw materials that went into it:

| Product | Recipe (4 items, same tier) | Raw Material Cost (approx., 4 items at that tier) | Product Base Value | Margin |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Small Hunt Product | 4 Small, 2+ Hunt | ~10–12gp | 14gp | +2–4gp |
| Medium Hunt Product | 4 Medium, 2+ Hunt | ~22–24gp | 28gp | +4–6gp |
| Large Hunt Product | 4 Large, 2+ Hunt | ~38–42gp | 48gp | +6–10gp |

(Fish/Forage/Mine Products follow the same shape — roughly a 15–25% markup over raw cost, scaling up at Large.) That margin is the entire reason to spend rounds crafting instead of just selling raw materials straight off the cart — it's not huge, but it's consistent, and it's the only way a Product exists at all.

Every other method on this floor — Gathering, Robbing, Trading, Scavenging, Favors — produces only **raw Small/Medium/Large/Huge-tier materials** from the four Gathering Tables. **Huge-tier materials are gathering-exclusive** — no other method can ever produce one. It's the only door to the best stuff, and the only thing that makes showing up to a Gathering Window on time worth the rigidity of the schedule.

