## PROCUREMENT SYSTEM

Roles are not fixed — any party member can Gather, Rob, Trade, Craft, Vend, Scout, Advertise, Perform, or Sabotage on any given day. The only standing rule is that **someone must be at a stall during the Selling Phase** (Rule 4).

There are four gathering tables, each producing results in four tiers: **Small, Medium, Large, Huge.** The flavor changes per table, but tier is what matters for crafting and combining.

### Gathering (Major Action)

**Cost:** the full window — 36 rounds, all RAP committed, no partial attendance. You must be present at the window's opening round; arriving even one round late forfeits that window entirely.

Each window pairs two tables and the category obtained is randomized per item (see Step 3). Each resource category appears in exactly **two** windows per day:

| Category | Windows |
|---|---|
| Hunt | A, D |
| Forage | A, C |
| Mine | B, D |
| Fish | B, C |

**Step 1 — Quality (rolled once, sets the tier for your whole session):** make the four listed skill checks for the table against DC 18 each.

| Successes (of 4) | Tier |
|---|---|
| 4 | Huge |
| 2–3 | Large |
| 1 | Medium |
| 0 | Small |

If any of the four d20s came in below 10, drop the result one stage (floor: Small).

**Step 2 — Quantity (crowding + depletion):**

| Players sharing this window/location | Draws |
|---|---|
| 1 | 5 |
| 2 | 4 |
| 3 | 3 |
| 4 | 2 |
| 5+ | 1 each |

**Depletion:** if this is the *second* window today in which this category has been gathered by anyone in the party (party-wide tracking), apply both: Draws −2 (minimum 1), and Tier capped at Large even if Step 1 produced Huge. Resets every morning.

**Step 3 — Category (per item):** roll 1d2 per draw to determine which of the window's two paired tables that item comes from.

**Skill checks per table:**

- **Forage:** Survival (the trek), Perception (the search), Nature (the verification), Medicine (the extraction)
- **Hunt:** Survival (the pursuit), Nature (the ambush), Animal Handling (the trap), Stealth (the approach)
- **Fish:** Nature (the read), Survival (the preparation), Perception (the stakeout), Sleight of Hand (the catch)
- **Mine:** Nature (the scout), Perception (the spot), Investigation (the analysis), Athletics (the strike) — Underground only, 1-in-6 Syndicate Enforcer encounter unless Stealth DC 13 is passed before descending.

