### Combine Action

Major Action (2 rounds, no check): combine 2 same-tier, same-table items into 1 item of the next tier up (2 Small→1 Medium, 2 Medium→1 Large, 2 Large→1 Huge). Costs a Major Action regardless of who performs it, so over-combining instead of gathering fresh has a genuine time cost.

### Crafting: Products

Each **Product** requires **four items of the same tier**, at least two from that Product's home table. The other two may be from any table, at that same tier.

| Product | Recipe | Tool | Base Value (Small / Medium / Large) |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Hunt Product** | 4 of one tier, 2+ from Hunt | Cook's, Leatherworker's, or Smith's Tools | 14gp / 28gp / 48gp |
| **Fish Product** | 4 of one tier, 2+ from Fish | Cook's Utensils | 12gp / 24gp / 42gp |
| **Forage Product** | 4 of one tier, 2+ from Forage | Potter's, Weaver's, or Herbalism Kit | 13gp / 26gp / 45gp |
| **Mine Product** | 4 of one tier, 2+ from Mine | Smith's or Jeweler's Tools | 16gp / 32gp / 55gp |

Huge-tier items don't feed standard Products — they're rare enough to go straight to Soren for identification, get used one-for-one as a flashy display item, or (DM discretion) substitute for an entire tier-down recipe slot — 1 Huge can count as "2 Large."

A player without proficiency in the relevant tool may attempt the check at **disadvantage**.

| Check Result | Quality | Sale Modifier |
|---|---|---|
| Failed by 5 or more | Ruined | Item destroyed; materials lost |
| Failed by 1–4 | Rough | −25% of base value |
| Passed | Standard | Base value |
| Passed by 4+ | Good | +35% of base value |
| Passed by 8+ | Excellent | +80% of base value |
| Natural 20 | Masterwork | +150% of base value; triggers a Special Customer roll |

The Product's name and flavor at the table is whatever fits the actual ingredients — a Large Hunt Product made from boar, deer, river clay, and herb sprigs might be called a "Game Hunter's Platter." Mechanically identical; narratively whatever the table wants.

