## REPUTATION TRACKER

Tracks standing in Verath's Crossing. Starts at **0**, range **−10 to +10**. Governs three things: how many customers show up, how much they're willing to pay before any negotiation, and which negotiation tools are even available. The lower it gets, the less of the market you have access to.

| Score | Customer Modifier | Base Price Modifier | Tool Access | Deception Discovery Modifier |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **+6 to +10** | +1d6 customers; vendors 15% better rates; 1 guaranteed Special Customer | **+15%** | All tools available | −15% discovery chance |
| **+3 to +5** | +1d4 customers; vendors 5% better | **+8%** | All tools available | −8% |
| **+1 to +2** | minor positive recognition | **+3%** | All tools available | −3% |
| **0** | neutral | — | All tools available | — |
| **−1 to −2** | slight wariness | **−5%** | Luxury Upsell DC +2 | +5% |
| **−3 to −5** | −1d4 customers; 2 vendors refuse to sell to you | **−12%** | Luxury Upsell unavailable; standard Upsell DC +2 | +12% |
| **−6 to −9** | −1d6 customers; most vendors wary; authority watching | **−25%** | Negotiation locked entirely — customers only accept Honest Sale at listed price | +20% |
| **−10** | stall shut down for 1 full day, pending inquiry | — | Cannot sell | — |

Base Price Modifier applies to a stall's listed prices before any negotiation check, and stacks with the day's Market Trend (e.g. a Liked category at +6 Reputation sells at roughly +45%; a Disliked category at −6 Reputation drops to roughly half price).

