## PRICE MANIPULATION — Persuasion, Deception, Intimidation

Used during the Selling Phase, once per customer, to push a sale above the listed price. DCs below are base values — apply Tool Access restrictions and the Deception Discovery Modifier from the Reputation Tracker on top of them.

| Method | Skill | DC | On Success | On Failure |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Honest Sale | — | — | Listed price guaranteed | — |
| Upsell (markup ≤30%) | Persuasion | 10 + markup% | Full marked-up price | Customer pays base price only |
| Luxury Upsell (markup 31–60%) | Persuasion | 14 + markup% | Full marked-up price | Customer walks (roll d6: 5–6, they buy from a rival instead) |
| Storytelling | Performance | 12 | +15% flat, stacks with Upsell | Sale proceeds at listed price, no bonus |
| Misrepresent Quality | Deception | 14 | Full inflated price now | Caught on the spot — sale fails, Reputation −1, next 1d4 customers this phase are wary (−1 to your negotiation checks) |
| Misrepresent Rarity | Deception | 15 | Full inflated price now | Caught on the spot — sale fails, Reputation −2, same wariness effect |
| Pressure Sell | Intimidation | 15 | Full price guaranteed | Customer leaves offended — −1d4 customers for the rest of the phase |

**Pressure Sell costs Reputation −1 per use, cumulative same day, whether it succeeds or fails.**

**Deception that succeeds isn't free.** Every successful Misrepresent Quality or Misrepresent Rarity sale carries a delayed Discovery chance, checked once at the end of the day (apply the Reputation Tracker's Discovery Modifier):

| Method | Base Discovery Chance | If Discovered |
|---|---|---|
| Misrepresent Quality | 25% | Reputation −1, customer demands a refund (lose that sale's gold) |
| Misrepresent Rarity | 35% | Reputation −2, customer demands a refund (lose that sale's gold) |

A trusted merchant gets away with the occasional lie because nobody's looking for it. Reputation that's already shaky makes every lie more likely to be caught — and getting caught is what drags Reputation into the range where Tool Access locks negotiation out entirely.

