## THE SELLING PHASE

Market Time runs 6:00–10:00. It is not round-counted — it continues until that day's customers are processed. Players **at their stall** handle customers; players **not at their stall** may spend RAP on interference, last-minute advertising, or sabotage, but cannot start Major Actions.

### How Many Customers Per Day

Base is **1d6+3 per stall**, modified by everything below — but for pacing across a 5-day floor, here's the intended curve:

| Day | Suggested Base | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Day 1 | 1d4+3 (4–7) | No reputation built yet; deliberately the slowest day |
| Day 2 | 1d6+3 (4–9) | Standard baseline |
| Day 3 | 1d6+3 (4–9), −1d4 all stalls (Grey Ledger opens) | Real competition arrives |
| Day 4 | 1d6+4 (5–10) | Word of mouth and accumulated Reputation start paying off |
| Day 5 | 1d8+4 (5–12); +2d8 if Vael is defeated | Climax day — biggest crowd of the floor |

A well-advertised, high-Reputation stall can comfortably push past 15–18 customers in a single phase. For table pacing, fully roleplay only the unusual ones (Special Customers, Syndicate interruptions below) — resolve routine customers (village child, farm laborer, etc.) with a quick price-and-roll rather than a full scene.

**Modifiers (tracked throughout the day):**

| Source | Modifier |
|---|---|
| Posted sign or flyer (each active) | +1d4 |
| Live demonstration completed | +2d4 |
| Shout / barter cry performed | +1d4 |
| Street crier hired (5gp) | +1d6 |
| Masterwork item visibly displayed at stall | +1d6 |
| Reputation modifier | see Reputation Tracker |
| Slanderer active and not countered | −1d6 |
| Rival sabotaged this day (their loss = your traffic) | +1d4 |
| Grey Ledger stall open (Day 3 onward) | −1d4 all stalls |

**If a customer walks after a failed upsell:** Roll d6. On a 5 or 6, they purchase from a rival stall instead (DM assigns the sale).

