## THE FLOOR BOSS: VAEL GELDRUN, THE CORRUPTED ARBITRATOR

### Lore

Vael Geldrun was Verath's Crossing's most respected Trade Arbitrator for eleven years. He resolved disputes fairly, held both sides accountable, and treated the town's covenant of honest commerce as something worth protecting.

The Iron Ledger approached him on a slow Tuesday with an offer he refused.

They came back. Then again. Then with evidence of a debt he had not paid — fabricated, but documented convincingly. Then with a quiet question about where a certain sum of money had gone. The question did not need to be true to be dangerous.

He accepted the arrangement. That was eleven years ago.

The Hollow Ledger's power runs through him now like a second circulatory system. He senses every transaction within the town's boundaries — the weight of coin, the pressure of unfulfilled promises, the faint friction of an honest sale. He experiences corruption the way other people experience warmth: sustaining.

He sits in his arbitrator's tower at the market's edge and does not appear to anyone. He watches. The Iron Ledger prospers.

He has forgotten what the covenant felt like. He has not forgotten what it cost him to break it.

### Boss Unlock Conditions

All four must be satisfied. Vael cannot be confronted until every condition is met.

| # | Condition | How to Complete |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Total earnings across all stalls reach **150gp cumulative** | Tracked across all five days |
| 2 | **3 Syndicate agents** have been publicly exposed | Tax Collector, Slanderer, Counterfeit Ring, Arsonist, Edrin Voss, or Mark-Hunter — any three |
| 3 | **The Iron Ledger Charter** has been discovered | Underground only; Find Iron Ledger Charter Major Action (DC 16) |
| 4 | **The Grey Ledger stall is open** | Opens automatically on Day 3; must still be operating |

When all four conditions are met at the start of Day 5, Vael is present when the players arrive at the market square.

### The Confrontation

> *The market square is quieter than usual when you arrive. Customers who were milling about have stepped back without being asked. The fountain basin reflects nothing useful.*
>
> *The man standing at the center is unremarkable at first — plain arbitrator's robes, ink-stained hands, a ledger under one arm. He is reading it. He does not look up for several seconds.*
>
> *When he does, his eyes are the color of tarnished silver.*
>
> *"You have been disrupting my market," he says. Not an accusation. A notation. "Most climbers find the economics discouraging and leave by Day 3."*
>
> *He closes the ledger.*
>
> *"I'm going to offer you the same arrangement I offer everyone. Walk away with what you have. Don't ask about what runs underneath. Both of us benefit from the simplicity."*
>
> *He looks at each of you in turn.*
>
> *"Or don't. The Ledger accommodates that outcome as well."*

**Option A — Accept:** Floor clears immediately. No boss rewards. Rankings based on earnings only.

**Option B — Refuse:** Vael severs the bazaar's protection rules. The market square transforms. Prices bleed from every surface. Numbers replace cobblestones. The air tastes of iron.

